Dev app consult — DONE

## A. Variant mechanism

**Known fix:** Google describes **product flavors** for separate Play listings with different application IDs. A release-like `dev` build type with `.dev` is also supported, but it represents a build configuration rather than a product edition. Flavors rename tasks to names such as `testDevReleaseUnitTest`; a new build type preserves existing `debug` and `release` tasks and adds `testDevUnitTest`, `bundleDev`, and `lintDev`. Source sets follow the same names. BuildConfig values are variant-specific. A custom build type needs `matchingFallbacks` when a **dependent library module** lacks that type. [Android build variants](https://developer.android.com/build/build-variants), [Android lint](https://developer.android.com/studio/write/lint).

**Today:** There are no flavors; only the opt-in debug suffix exists ([app/build.gradle.kts](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/build.gradle.kts:40)). `settings.gradle.kts` includes `llama-android` and `accelerator-benchmark`, but the listed app dependencies declare no `project(...)` dependency on either ([settings.gradle.kts](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/settings.gradle.kts:17), [app/build.gradle.kts](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/build.gradle.kts:113)). Their own variants are **UNCHECKED**. Release has no Gradle signing or R8 shrinking configuration in the listed file. The release script signs the resulting unsigned bundle separately ([build.sh](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/scripts/release/build.sh:15), [publish.py](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/scripts/release/publish.py:74)).

**Traps:** `initWith(release)` does not create a signing key or turn on R8 when release has neither configured. Flavor task renames affect the stated roughly 90 references; the listed CI still expects `testDebugUnitTest` reports and `bundleRelease` ([pr-check.yml](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/.github/workflows/pr-check.yml:50), [build.sh](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/scripts/release/build.sh:15)). Actual `testDevUnitTest` and `lintDev` execution: **NOT VERIFIED**.

## B. Five-process file logging

**Known fix:** Android documents process-unique rotating files as supported `FileHandler` behavior. It gives **no canonical five-process shared-log recipe**. Its append API explicitly says atomic end-of-file writes across programs are *filesystem-specific*; it promises no complete-line size limit. Keep disk work off capture and UI threads. Use a boot-relative clock for cross-process intervals; wall time can change. [FileHandler](https://developer.android.com/reference/java/util/logging/FileHandler), [append semantics](https://developer.android.com/reference/java/nio/file/StandardOpenOption), [StrictMode](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/StrictMode), [SystemClock](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/SystemClock).

**Today:** `DebugLogger` writes only to logcat ([DebugLogger.kt](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/debug/DebugLogger.kt:76)); five processes are declared ([AndroidManifest.xml](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:81)). Its pipeline clock is per-process state ([DebugLogger.kt](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/debug/DebugLogger.kt:36)). Given the verified `:audio`-only start, marks in main and `:asr` report device uptime. The verified take-ID gaps at ASR initialization and polish also impede correlation.

**Traps:** One shared `O_APPEND` file does not guarantee intact lines; concurrent rotation can strand writers on old files. Synchronous writes or `fsync` can delay capture or insertion. A background queue avoids that delay but can lose pending lines on process death. Per-process files need explicit cross-file ordering; wall timestamps alone are unsafe.

## C. Logging switch across processes

**Known patterns:** A build constant is fixed per variant. AIDL or a `ContentProvider` crosses process boundaries; a file flag needs cross-process consistency rules. Android’s supported shared-preference-store route is `MultiProcessDataStoreFactory`, with **all** readers of that file using the multi-process form. [AIDL](https://developer.android.com/develop/background-work/services/aidl), [providers](https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/providers/content-providers), [DataStore](https://developer.android.com/topic/libraries/architecture/datastore).

**Today:** The listed preferences use single-process `preferencesDataStore` ([AppPreferences.kt](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/settings/AppPreferences.kt:22)); per the verified fact, only main reads it. No logging switch appears in its first 120 lines.

**Traps:** A file flag can be stale or partially updated; a provider adds IPC and startup behavior; an AIDL setting can miss events before binding or after process restart; a BuildConfig constant cannot act as a live toggle. Reading this existing DataStore independently in helpers would violate Android’s single-versus-multi-process rule.

## D. Sharing a log

**Known fix:** `FileProvider` supplies a `content://` URI with temporary read permission for a share intent. Variant-specific `${applicationId}.fileprovider` avoids authority collision. `file://` sharing fails for targets such as Gmail. Gmail’s personal-account attachment limit is 25 MB; other targets vary. [Android file sharing](https://developer.android.com/training/secure-file-sharing), [FileProvider setup](https://developer.android.com/training/secure-file-sharing/setup-sharing), [Gmail Help](https://support.google.com/mail/answer/6584).

**Today:** Neither listed manifest declares a `FileProvider` ([main manifest](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:23), [debug manifest](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/debug/AndroidManifest.xml:3)).

**Traps:** A literal authority collides across the two apps. Sharing an actively written file may yield an incomplete archive. A large zip may be rejected or converted to a cloud link by the chosen target.

## E. Compile-out

**Known fix:** Variant source sets can include code only in the Dev build; R8 can remove unreachable constant-gated code when optimization is enabled. An AAB exposes its manifest and DEX for inspection. Source-set exclusion is the stronger packaging boundary; a no-op class must not duplicate the same class in `main`. [Source sets](https://developer.android.com/build/build-variants), [R8](https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/app-optimization/enable-app-optimization), [AAB format](https://developer.android.com/guide/app-bundle/app-bundle-format).

**Today:** The shared logger is in `main` and has no file sink ([DebugLogger.kt](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/debug/DebugLogger.kt:16)). The shape test forbids `FileWriter`/`Environment` there and scans `main`, `debug`, and `androidTest` for content-bearing diagnostic shapes ([DiagnosticsShapeTest.kt](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/test/java/com/envi/wispr/debug/DiagnosticsShapeTest.kt:46), [DiagnosticsShapeTest.kt](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/test/java/com/envi/wispr/debug/DiagnosticsShapeTest.kt:82)). No built Consumer AAB was inspected: **NOT VERIFIED**.

**Traps:** A BuildConfig boolean alone leaves code in an unshrunk bundle. Even an AAB search for file APIs or strings cannot prove the absence of every possible content-bearing call; the current test is shape-based and documents limits ([DiagnosticsShapeTest.kt](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/test/java/com/envi/wispr/debug/DiagnosticsShapeTest.kt:28)).

## F. Both apps installed

**Known fix:** Android allows multiple accessibility services to be enabled, so each app’s service must be considered separately. Assist selection is a device/default-app choice. Distinct task affinities prevent cross-app task grouping; distinct visible labels identify tiles and channels. [Accessibility services](https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/ui/accessibility/views/service), [task affinity](https://developer.android.com/guide/components/activities/tasks-and-back-stack), [Quick Settings tiles](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/views/quicksettings-tiles), [notification channels](https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/compose/notifications/channels).

**Today:** The shared manifest declares the accessibility service, `ACTION_ASSIST`, and a tile literally labeled `EnviousWispr` ([AndroidManifest.xml](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:119), [AndroidManifest.xml](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:67), [AndroidManifest.xml](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:132)). `VoiceInputActivity` hardcodes the same affinity for both packages ([AndroidManifest.xml](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:64)); the guide activity already uses `${applicationId}` ([AndroidManifest.xml](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:38)).

**Traps:** Both accessibility services could react to one interaction. Two Assist handlers compete for selection; actual Samsung side-button behavior is **NOT VERIFIED**. The shared affinity can mix tasks, and identical tile labels confuse selection. Notification-channel names live outside the allowed files: **UNCHECKED**.

## G. Telemetry

**Known fix:** Treat app edition and debuggability as separate facts. `FLAG_DEBUGGABLE` describes whether the build is debuggable, not whether its Play listing is Dev. [Android build types](https://developer.android.com/build/building-cmdline).

**Today:** `TelemetryConfig` maps every non-debuggable build to `production` ([TelemetryConfig.kt](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/telemetry/TelemetryConfig.kt:33)). Thus a Play-publishable Dev bundle would report production. The environment is exposed by `Telemetry.status()` and the config is passed into Sentry and PostHog bootstrap ([Telemetry.kt](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/telemetry/Telemetry.kt:61), [Telemetry.kt](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/telemetry/Telemetry.kt:79)). Their exact downstream use of `environment` is **UNCHECKED** because their bootstrap files were not allowed. The release identifier *does* use `BuildConfig.APPLICATION_ID`, so the two packages would have distinct release prefixes ([TelemetryConfig.kt](/Users/m4pro_sv/Developer/EnviousLabs/EnviousWispr-Android/.claude/worktrees/378-dev-app-local-log/app/src/main/java/com/envi/wispr/telemetry/TelemetryConfig.kt:23)).